    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6256" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">călĭgātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		caliga, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>wearing soldiers</i>' <i>boots</i>, <i>booted</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Dig. 3, 2, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">48, 3, 9</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 279,
			3</span></i>.—Of a peasant <i>in heavy
			shoes</i>, <i>brogans</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 3,
			322</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">călĭgātus</span></b> ,
			i, m. (sc. miles), <i>a
				common soldier</i>, <i>a private</i>, =
			gregarius, <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 25</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Dig. 27,
				1, 10</span></i>.</div>
